<template name="tus_settings_gui_Machinedrum">
<head>
	<style>
		.settings-os-actions {
			display: flex;
			flex-direction: column;
			gap: 6dp;
			width: 100%;
		}
		.settings-os-actions .button {
			display: block;
			box-sizing: border-box;
			width: 100%;
		}
		.settings-os-actions .button:disabled {
			opacity: 0.45;
		}
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<h1>Panel Rendering</h1>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<div id="btPixelPerfectPanel" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
		<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
		<label>Crisp LCD and panel lines (experimental)</label>
	</div>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<label>Use whole-pixel LCD enlargement and align thin panel lines to pixels. Changes immediately; the LCD may appear smaller with more space around it.</label>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<div id="btLcdRotaryInteraction" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
		<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
		<label>Drag and scroll rotary controls shown on the LCD</label>
	</div>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<label>Works on synthesis parameters, LFO edit, and Master FX. Menus, tabs, empty cells, and other LCD controls remain inert.</label>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<div id="btHostButtonsTap" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
		<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
		<label>MIDI-mapped panel buttons tap</label>
	</div>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<label>On: switching a panel button parameter on is one short press, and the plugin switches it back off right after, so every mapped note in Ableton Live is one press and the parameter shows Off when the key is up. Off: 1 holds the button and 0 releases it, for momentary CC buttons, held trigs and parameter locks. Clicks in the plugin window always behave like the hardware.</label>

	<settingsspacer1/>
	<h1>Panel MIDI</h1>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<label>A MIDI controller on this channel plays the front panel: keys, trigs and the endless encoders, page by page like the hardware. Nothing on this channel reaches the machine, and encoder movement never shows up in host automation; the machine reports the parameters it changes instead. Right-click a key or encoder on the panel to learn a control. Input comes from the track's MIDI and from the MIDI input chosen on the MIDI page.</label>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<label>Channel</label>
		<table class="settings-table">
			<tr class="settings-tr">
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannelOff" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>Off</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel1" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>1</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel2" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>2</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel3" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>3</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel4" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>4</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel5" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>5</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel6" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>6</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel7" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>7</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel8" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>8</label>
					</div>
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr class="settings-tr">
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel9" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>9</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel10" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>10</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel11" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>11</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel12" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>12</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel13" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>13</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel14" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>14</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel15" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>15</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiChannel16" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>16</label>
					</div>
				</td>
			</tr>
		</table>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<label id="lbPanelMidiChannelInfo"></label>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<label>Encoder CC format</label>
		<table class="settings-table">
			<tr class="settings-tr">
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiEncodingTwosComplement" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>Relative (two's complement)</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiEncodingBinaryOffset" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>Relative (offset 64)</label>
					</div>
				</td>
			</tr>
			<tr class="settings-tr">
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiEncodingSignMagnitude" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>Relative (signed bit)</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btPanelMidiEncodingAbsolute" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>Absolute knob</label>
					</div>
				</td>
			</tr>
		</table>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<div class="settings-panelmidi-actions">
		<button id="btPanelMidiForgetAll" class="button">Forget All Panel MIDI Mappings</button>
	</div>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<label id="lbPanelMidiMappingCount"></label>

	<settingsspacer1/>
	<h1>Operating System</h1>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<label>Install an OS from an Elektron OS upgrade file (.syx). In the background the plugin starts the machine's own bootloader (EARLY STARTUP MENU, MIDI UPGRADE), sends the file and saves the programmed flash as an 8 MiB .bin image. This takes a few minutes. The stock .bin is still needed as the base.</label>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<label id="lbOsRunning"></label>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<div class="settings-os-actions">
		<button id="btOsInstall" class="button">Install OS from .syx...</button>
		<button id="btOsCancel" class="button">Cancel Installation</button>
		<button id="btOsChoose" class="button">Use Installed OS...</button>
		<button id="btOsStock" class="button">Use Stock OS</button>
	</div>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<label id="lbOsInstallStatus"></label>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<label>Switching restarts the machine and keeps kits, patterns and songs. Samples in flash (MD-UW samples, MM DigiPRO waves) are not carried over; reload the project after switching back. The emulation is tuned for OS 1.63; other OS versions are untested and may misbehave.</label>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<h1>RAM Recording</h1>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<div id="btRamRecordingComplete" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
		<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
		<label>Complete RAM recording tails (recommended)</label>
	</div>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<label>Writes the complete advertised recording extent, preventing old audio from remaining at the end of some recordings.</label>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<div id="btRamRecordingOriginal" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
		<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
		<label>Original RAM recording finalization</label>
	</div>
	<settingsspacer1/>
	<label>Preserves the original OS 1.63 recording logic for exact compatibility.</label>

	<settingsspacer1/>
	<div class="settings-advanced">
		<h1>Panel Feel</h1>
		<settingsspacer1/>
		<label>Sound selection wheel speed</label>
		<table class="settings-table">
			<tr class="settings-tr">
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btWheelSpeed50" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>50%</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btWheelSpeed75" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>75%</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btWheelSpeed100" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>100%</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btWheelSpeed150" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>150%</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btWheelSpeed200" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>200%</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btWheelSpeed300" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>300%</label>
					</div>
				</td>
			</tr>
		</table>
		<settingsspacer1/>
		<label>Data entry encoder speed</label>
		<table class="settings-table">
			<tr class="settings-tr">
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btEncoderSpeed50" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>50%</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btEncoderSpeed75" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>75%</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btEncoderSpeed100" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>100%</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btEncoderSpeed150" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>150%</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btEncoderSpeed200" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>200%</label>
					</div>
				</td>
				<td class="settings-td">
					<div id="btEncoderSpeed300" class="settings-checkboxwithlabel">
						<button id="button" class="settings-checkbox"/>
						<label>300%</label>
					</div>
				</td>
			</tr>
		</table>
	</div>
	<settingsspacer1/>
</body>
</template>
